    <!-- Privacy statement (same as PRIVACY.md) -->
    <string name="privacy_short">Your data never leaves your phone. The app cannot connect to the internet.</string>
    <string name="privacy_reads_title">What the app reads</string>
    <string name="privacy_reads">• Step counts and walking distance from Health Connect, only for the times of your own sessions. It reads no other health data and never writes to Health Connect.\n• NFC tags that you tap, to recognise which pair you are wearing. It only reads a random code it wrote to the tag itself and ignores everything else.</string>
    <string name="privacy_stores_title">What the app stores</string>
    <string name="privacy_stores">On your phone only, in the app\'s private storage: your pairs (name, brand, model, type, price, purchase date, colour), your sessions (start and end times, time zone, step counts and distances) and your settings (such as the default currency). The app does not collect your location, contacts, photos or any identifier of you or your phone.</string>
    <string name="privacy_shares_title">What the app shares</string>
    <string name="privacy_shares">Nothing. The app has no internet permission, no accounts, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking libraries. Its data is left out of Android cloud backups and device transfers. The only way data leaves the app is when you export a CSV file to a place you pick.</string>
    <string name="privacy_delete_title">Deleting your data</string>
    <string name="privacy_delete">Delete a pair to remove it and its sessions, or uninstall the app to remove everything. You can stop step and distance reading at any time in Health Connect.</string>

